      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>Legionella risk is managed under the Health and Safety at Work etc Act 1974, the L8 ACOP and HSG274.</li><li>A school with a water system needs a risk assessment. Where there is risk, it needs a written scheme of routine checks.</li><li>The holidays are the peak risk. Taps sit unused and the water goes stale.</li><li>The log does not control legionella. The scheme, carried out, does.</li><li>Quickler flags a reading that is out of range and lists it as a job.</li></ul>"
    },
